From 4dec5b60f97bdddf60a07ae3f2a8e75713b5b65f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raza <raza@bukc.edu.pk>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:34:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): password security hardening, coordinator invite
 audit log, Profile/MyBorrows cleanup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Several fixes and one feature, all from direct feedback.

1. INVITE-COORDINATOR VALIDATION GAP (the actual cause of the reported
   all-zero contact number). inviteCoordinatorSchema still had the old
   loose z.string().min(5).max(30) contact-number check — never updated
   when the strict Pakistani-format validation was added to student/
   external registration. Fixed: same strict schemas now apply here too.

2. PASSWORD RESET/CHANGE HARDENING (AUTH-21 + the listed security rules).
   The 'email says 7 days' turned out to be the coordinator invite email
   (a separate, correctly-7-day flow) — the actual reset email has
   always correctly said 15 minutes. What WAS missing:
   - Rate limiting: max 3 reset requests per email / 10 per IP per
     15-minute window (new password_reset_attempt table, migration 017).
     Rate-limited requests get the exact same generic response as
     'no such account' — no signal either way.
   - 'Only the latest link works': requesting a new reset now
     invalidates any earlier still-live token for that user.
   - Confirmation email sent after BOTH a reset and a self-service
     change ('your password was changed, if this wasn't you...').
   - change-password now shares the reset-attempt rate-limit counter
     (a burst of wrong-current-password guesses and a burst of
     forgot-password spam are both attacks on the same account).
   Deliberately NOT done: converting change-password into an email-link
   flow. AUTH-17 is explicit that a logged-in user proves identity with
   their current password — a different, already-valid identity proof
   than what the reset token exists for. Same security posture
   (rate-limited, session-invalidated, alerted) without merging the two
   mechanisms — see the chat writeup for the reasoning.
   Also hit and worked around a pre-existing Kysely/TypeScript quirk:
   inequality comparisons against Generated<Timestamp> columns don't
   typecheck anywhere in the codebase (confirmed on the older
   login_attempt table too, not something introduced here) — routed
   around it with the same raw-sql pattern already proven in the
   account-search query.

3. COORDINATOR INVITE AUDIT LOG. New 'Coordinator Invitations Sent'
   panel in Admin Accounts — every invite ever sent, who sent it, when,
   and its status (Pending / Accepted / Expired). The coordinator_invite
   table already had everything needed; this is the read side.

4. PROFILE SCREEN: removed the Contact row (unreliable data, not worth
   surfacing) — Personal Details now shows Full Name, Email, and
   role-specific fields only.

5. STUDENT BORROW HISTORY MOVED FULLY TO PROFILE. MyBorrowsScreen no
   longer duplicates the request list — it's the dedicated 'submit a
   request' screen now, with a pointer to Profile for history. Profile's
   Borrowing Activity section replaced its simple name+status row with
   the full Equipment/Window/Status/Note table (matching the screenshot),
   showing the complete history rather than a 5-item preview, since
   Profile is now the only place this lives.

Tests: 6 new in auth.test.ts covering rate limiting (both that it fires
and that it stays silent to the caller either way), only-latest-token
invalidation, session-kill-on-reset, the exact reported contact-number
bug now rejected, and the invite audit log's Pending->Accepted
transition. Fixed 3 test files whose coordinator-invite fullName helpers
embedded a digit (same issue fixed for student registration earlier,
now needed here too since invite-coordinator's name validation is
strict). Fixed one bug in my own T-125d test (forgot to verify the
account before asserting login succeeds).

Verified against a real local Postgres: migrations 001-017 apply
cleanly, seed runs, tsc --noEmit clean on both sides, auth suite 59/59.
Full cross-suite run: 139/143 — the 4 failures are the same pre-existing
Asia/Karachi same-day timing flake identified earlier in this project
(confirmed via byte-identical date logic diff against origin), more
visible than usual right now because the test run landed well past
midnight in Karachi, which is exactly the condition that triggers it.
